            "number": "1",
            "title": "It might not \"just be colic\"",
            "body": "<p>You've tried burping mid-feed, switching formula, slower-flow nipples — and your baby still seems uncomfortable after most feeds. Most parents assume it's just \"normal baby stuff\" that they have to wait out.</p><p>What rarely comes up: the bottle itself — both the material and how much air the design lets your baby swallow — can be part of what's making feeds harder than they need to be. It's worth ruling out before assuming it's something you just have to live with.</p>"
          }
        },
